## Card Image Quality Strategy (Critical)

### Asset Spec

| Asset | Resolution | Format | Notes |
|-------|------------|--------|-------|
| Master art | **512 × 839** px per card | PNG (lossless) | Wikimedia hanafuda aspect (~0.61) |
| `@3x` | 512 × 839 | PNG | Primary source for phones |
| `@2x` | 341 × 560 | PNG | Generated from master |
| `@1x` | 171 × 280 | PNG | Thumbnail / low-memory |
| Card back | 512 × 839 | PNG | `back/card-back.png` (+ @2x/@3x) |

### Rendering Rules

- Use **`expo-image`** (not bare `Image`) for disk cache + transition
- **Never** upscale beyond `@3x` — always ship sharp source art
- Table cards: **56×91pt** display (`CARD_DIMENSIONS.table`; was 60×97 → 64×103)
- Hand cards: **64×104pt** display (`CARD_DIMENSIONS.hand`; was 68×110 → 72×116)
- Opponent face-down hand: **mini** size **22×36pt** (compact fan above collected piles)
- Provide **subtle drop shadow** via wrapper View, not baked into PNG (keeps assets reusable)
- **Border radius** applied in CSS (`borderRadius: 6`) — do not bake rounded corners into master PNG

