## Play Model — Human vs AI

This app is **always Human vs AI**. There is no couch co-op or hot-seat multiplayer.

| Role | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Human** | One local player — hand at bottom, full touch control |
| **AI** | All other seats — automated turns, visible collected piles & scores |

### Session layout

| Mode | Korean | Seats | Hand | Table | Target | Ship in |
|------|--------|-------|------|-------|--------|---------|
| **Matgo** (default) | 맞고 | Human + **1 AI** | 10 each | 8 | **7** | **Phase 2** |
| **Go-Stop** | 고스톱 | Human + **2 AI** | 7 each | 6 | **3** | **Phase 4** ✅ |
| **Hwatu Simple** | 화투 심플 | Human + **1 AI** | 10 each | 8 | per-card | **Phase 4** ✅ |

Settlement (고박·피박·광박) applies between human and AI opponent(s) using standard rules.

### AI difficulty

Selectable in **Settings** (default game mode + AI difficulty). Persist with AsyncStorage. Home **Play** launches `/game` with saved defaults.

| Level | Korean | English | Behavior (summary) |
|-------|--------|---------|-------------------|
| `beginner` | 초보 | Beginner | Obvious matches; weak yaku awareness; calls Stop early; occasional random plays |
| `intermediate` | 중급 | Intermediate | Solid matching; basic yaku chasing; reasonable Go/Stop |
| `advanced` | 고급 | Advanced | Optimizes yaku & pi; better match choice (싼 것 avoidance); strategic Go |
| `expert` | 전문가 | Expert | Strong lookahead; maximizes score & penalties; optimal Go/Stop; declares 흔들기/폭탄 when available |

Implementation: `src/game/ai.ts` + `AiDifficulty` type. Each level tunes weights / search depth / mistake rate — not separate codebases. **Hand/table match heuristics** for intermediate+ and expert are shared with turn hints via `src/game/hint.ts` (`getBestHandCard`, `getBestTableIndex`).

```ts
type AiDifficulty = 'beginner' | 'intermediate' | 'advanced' | 'expert';
```

### Turn hints (human assist) ✅

Optional **턴 힌트** — Settings → Gameplay → **Turn Hints** (`hintsEnabled`, default **on**, AsyncStorage).

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| `hint.ts` | `getTurnHint` — evaluates each legal hand play + table choice |
| `useMatgoGame` | Computes `turnHint` when `hintsEnabled` && human turn && `!isAnimating` |
| `HandFanView` / `CardView` | `hintedCardIds` / `hinted` — cyan (`#5CEFFF`) border + Reanimated pulse |
| `game.tsx` | Highlights suggested hand card and table slot (no text banner) |

**Hint evaluation (v2 — score + yaku progress):**

1. **Score delta** — simulate cards collected from hand play (not deck flip); `syncPlayerScore` before/after; includes bonus pi from 따닥·뻑·싼 것 when applicable
2. **Partial yaku bonus** — `countYakuProgress` weights incomplete godori·홍단·청단·초단 (completion already in score delta — no double count)
3. **Dump (no match)** — prefer lowest-type discard; penalize throwing yaku-relevant cards still needed for incomplete yaku

**Limitations (not in hint):** deck flip probability, opponent blocking, Go/Stop timing, 흔들기/폭탄 advice. Practical level ≈ **중급~중상급** assist, not pro-level lookahead.

